    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and reports metrics that can be trusted. It is written to be executed against a running system, with each item producing an artifact (log line, metric snapshot, or recorded output) that a reviewer can inspect.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every node in the cluster is running the exact same logical configuration, and that the configuration you think you're testing is the one actually deployed.\n\n### 1.1 Model artifact identity\n- [ ] Record the model's cryptographic hash (SHA-256 of weights, or the digest from the artifact registry) on **every node**, not just the coordinator. Compare across nodes; all must match.\n- [ ] Record tokenizer files (vocab, merges, special-tokens config) hashes separately. Tokenizer drift across nodes causes silent divergence in tokenized inputs.\n- [ ] Record the model revision/tag actually loaded at runtime (e.g., the resolved commit SHA, not the floating tag like `latest` or `main`).\n- [ ] Verify quantization settings (if any) are identical: quantization method, group size, calibration dataset identifier, and the hash of the quantized artifact itself.\n- [ ] Confirm that any sharded weight files (tensor-parallel shards) were produced from the same source checkpoint version \u2014 shard generation tool version should be logged.\n\n### 1.2 Runtime and framework identity\n- [ ] Log the serving framework version and its git commit (if built from source) on every node.\n- [ ] Log versions of the inference kernel stack (e.g., CUDA/cuDNN/NCCL versions, kernel library versions, compiler versions for any JIT-compiled kernels).\n- [ ] Verify driver and firmware",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
